ObjectBroker PRICING

The ObjectBroker product is Digital's preeminent CORBA/COM (Common Object
Model) software for legacy application integration, new application
development, and streamlined client/server computing across 11 platforms.
Now Digital is offering simplified, standardized pricing across all the
platforms, significant price reductions on the PC platforms, and flat
capacity licensing. These changes can be summarized as follows:

Before                                    Now

o  Digital Platforms

   Multitier runtime licenses		  Flat pricing per machine
   Personal plus multitier development	  Flat development licenses with
   					  aggressive discounts

o  Sun, HP, and IBM Platforms

   Inconsistent, flat runtime prices	  Consistent flat price per machine
   Flat development licensing with no 	  Flat development licenses with
   discount curve			  aggressive discounts

o  Windows, Windows NT, and Macintosh Platforms

   Flat runtime prices 			  Much lower flat runtime prices
   Varying flat development prices	  Consistent personal license with
   					  aggressive discounts and "QB"
   					  package prices

In essence, the tier structure on Digital platforms is being eliminated,
development licenses will be assigned to users at consistent prices across
UNIX and PC platforms, deeper discounts will be assigned to flat capacity
development licenses (standard pricing is still in effect on all runtime
licenses), and PC runtime prices are being slashed.

For more information on ObjectBroker and COM, please see the "Common Object
Model for ObjectBroker and OLE" article in the February 14, 1994, issue of
Digital's Customer Update.

