Digital 2100 Server Models A500MP and A600MP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Unmatched functionality, price/performance, and expandability

o  High performance, scalable SMP systems with variety of high availability
   solutions

o  Industry standard PCI and EISA I/O

o  Three-year onsite warranty

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital 2100 Server Models A500MP and A600MP are the first in a series
of affordable SMP, PCI based servers backed by a unique, three-year onsite
hardware warranty. They offer high availability features such as internal
RAID and hot swap disks, are highly scalable, and support the DEC OSF/1,
Microsoft's Windows NT Advanced Server, and OpenVMS operating systems.

Three Digital 2100 Server models are being offered: the Model A500MP
pedestal system, designed for the office environment; the Model A600MP
packaged system, providing higher expansion and additional high availability
features; and the Model A500MP-R space saving rackmount system (discussed in
an accompanying article).

The Model A600MP consists of at least one A500MP-R system plus rackmount
storage and other associated equipment mounted in a standard Digital
cabinet. With this system it is easier to create such high availability
configurations as a VAXcluster system for the OpenVMS platform, a DECsafe
configuration for the DEC OSF/1 platform, or other configurations that
require large amounts of storage. This is the package to choose when you
have large system requirements.

The chief Digital 2100 Server features are as follows:

o  System module -- The Digital 2100 Server is based on the DECchip 21064,
   running at 190 MHz. It will be easily upgradable to future generations of
   processors using the recently announced DECchip 21064A (275 MHz) and to
   future generations of DECchip technology.

   The server uses a high speed system bus as the primary interconnect
   between memory, CPUs, and the I/O subsystems. The bus has a bandwidth of
   667 Mbytes per second.

o  Memory -- 64 Mbyte, 128 Mbyte, and 512 Mbyte ECC memory modules are
   supported on the Digital 2100 Server, for a total of up to 2 Gbytes of
   memory (depending on the configuration).

o  System I/O -- Two I/O buses are standard on the base system: PCI and
   EISA:

   - PCI -- The Digital 2100 Server is the industry's first multiprocessor
     system to incorporate PCI (Peripheral Component Interconnect), the new
     PC industry standard I/O bus, which offers high performance (132 Mbytes
     per second) at commodity prices.

   - EISA -- By providing support for EISA (33 Mbytes per second), the most
     widely used server I/O bus, Digital 2100 Servers offer a wide range of
     inexpensive options with good performance.

o  SCSI -- The Digital 2100 Server also supports the multiple SCSI-2 (10
   Mbytes per second) buses and will support the FWD SCSI (20 Mbytes per
   second) controller in the near future.

o  Modular mass storage -- All Digital 2100 Server systems use the Digital
   StorageWorks backplane and modular storage devices. The Model A500MP
   pedestal system has one standard and one optional BA350 shelf, for a
   total of 16 internal devices. Each backplane is split into two separate
   SCSI buses. The Model A600MP packaged system includes one 3.5 inch
   internal system disk, and the rest of the mass storage in the cabinet
   comes on multiple, independently powered, rackmountable StorageWorks
   shelves.

   The use of the BA350 StorageWorks backplane provides commonality of
   storage options with other Digital systems and storage expansion systems,
   and also enables hot swap disks and easy user access to storage devices.

   Each Digital 2100 Server package supports a floppy diskette drive, a
   CDROM, and several variants of tape devices in two 5.25 inch half-height
   bays.

o  High availability product features:

   - Hot swap of disks.
   - Optional internal hardware RAID (levels 0, 1, 0+1, 5).
   - ECC protected memory and backup cache.
   - Optional redundant power source.
   - Auto restart and reconfiguration.
   - Internal temperature monitoring and control.
   - Optional external UPS.

o  Server management and diagnostics -- Sophisticated system diagnostics and
   fault management software stored in redundant, nonvolatile memory
   automatically identify failed system components and reconfigure the
   system to operate without them. An independent maintenance processor and
   a diagnostics control bus perform diagnostics of the major system
   components at system startup and then communicate results to the operator
   control panel. A menu driven interface and a powerful command set allow
   the system operator to monitor and manage every component of the system.
   All Digital 2100 Servers can be booted from a variety of local and
   network connected load devices. For distributed system operations,
   Digital is developing a set of integrated hardware and software system
   management solutions.

o  Investment protection for OpenVMS users -- Two optional devices are
   available to support DSSI configurations:

   - EISA/DSSI adapter (KFESA), which gives the system the capability of
     creating DSSI clusters.

   - The HSD05, which connects the StorageWorks SCSI disk drives to a DSSI
     bus, allowing these drives to be used in a DSSI OpenVMS cluster
     environment.

o  Table 1 lists base system features and compares the storage and power
   features of Models A500MP and A600MP.

   Table 1. Digital 2100 Server Base System, Storage, and Power Features

   Base System

   CPUs				  1 to 4
