Digital 2100 Server Model A500MP-R

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides same functionality as similarly configured pedestal system

o  Conforms to ANSI/EIA standard for 19 inch rackmount cabinets

o  Offers maximum flexibility and expandability

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The functionality of the Digital 2100 Server Model A500MP-R rackmount system
is identical to that of a similarly configured Digital 2100 Model A500MP
pedestal system (see the accompanying article in this issue). This is the
package to choose when your floor space is at a premium.

The Model A500MP-R rackmount system is 14 inches high, 17 inches wide, and
28 inches deep. It is designed to mount in standard, 19-inch-wide rails with
either RETMA or METRIC spacing on the mounting holes; cabling is in the
rear. The chassis is mounted on sliding rails for complete front access and
uses front-to-back cooling. (Two persons are required for installation.)

BENEFITS

In areas where the overhead cost of floor space is high, it is often more
cost-effective to use a cabinet system requiring a fixed amount of floor
space for all equipment. For example, an availability configuration such as
a VAXcluster system using the Digital 2100 Server Model A500MP-R rackmount
system takes up about one-half the amount of floor space of a comparable
pedestal configuration while providing more storage capability.

The Model A500MP-R supports redundant power supplies in an N+1 arrangement,
allowing a single power supply to support a fully loaded system. Other high
availability features available with packaged systems include dual AC power
controllers, optional rackmounted UPS systems, and redundant power supplies
for the StorageWorks shelves. All of these features, plus the ease of
maintaining and servicing the rackmount system, make it the obvious
building-block choice for your high availability requirements. If you have
high storage requirements, note that the Model A500MP-R can support up to 10
StorageWorks shelves in a single cabinet with 60 inches of usable space
(actual height is 67 inches). Other types of storage, such as DSSI, are also
available.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital 2100 Server Model A500MP-R rackmount system is orderable now.

