Digital 2100 A500TDS Technical Developer's System

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Complete, preconfigured system for technical application development on
   DEC OSF/1 AXP platform

o  First SMP system that can be used for both scalar and parallel
   application development, with one order number, at one low price

o  Allows easy integration and application development with AdvantageCluster
   Compute Servers (formerly Alpha AXP Packaged Farms)

o  Includes new products: DEC Fortran 90 and Digital Parallel Software
   Environment

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital 2100 A500TDS Technical Developer's System is a complete,
prepackaged system of hardware and software to satisfy the needs of the
technical application developer. It is a member of the new family of Digital
2100 A500MP systems, specially designed for symmetric multiprocessing (SMP).
The Digital 2100 A500TDS is based on the two-way Digital 2100 A500MP,
including ample memory, storage, and a full suite of development and
optimization tools for technical application developers.

Performance optimization tools include: the Digital Extended Math Library
(DXML) subroutines, used for high level math translations; KAP (Kuck &
Associates) preprocessor tools (in the new version supporting SMP) for
Fortran 77 and C compilers; DEC FUSE toolkits, which are Motif based
graphics tools for Fortran 77, C, and C++ application development; the C
Developer's Extensions toolkit (C compiler and UNIX development tools); and
DEC C++ and DEC Fortran (based on Fortran 77) compilers. This suite of
mature, integrated software products provides support for both scalar and
SMP application development. (For more information please refer to the
TechAdvantage article in this issue.)

The Digital 2100 A500TDS also includes Digital's newest software development
tools, DEC Fortran 90 and the Digital Parallel Software Environment. DEC
Fortran 90, the newest COHESION compiler, not only meets the ANSI and ISO
Fortran 90 standards but also supports the High Performance Fortran
Specification for parallelizing applications. The Digital Parallel Software
Environment provides runtime and testing support for parallelized
applications. These products can be used for both SMP and parallel
processing of applications. (Please refer to the accompanying articles for
more details.)

The Digital 2100 A500TDS is available with one order number, for one "less
than sum of the pieces" price: you obtain an easy-to-install, preconfigured
system that eliminates incomplete configurations and limited usability. The
system can be easily added to an existing network to increase application
performance as a centralized, powerful, scalable server or used to increase
single application performance with its multiple processors. Whether it's C
or Fortran, applications can utilize the software development tools to run
in parallel or ensure scalablity through SMP, leading to an overall increase
in application performance.

BENEFITS

o  Reliability -- Three year, onsite hardware warranty with next day, 24
   hour a day response.

o  Industry standards -- DEC OSF/1 (unified UNIX) and PCI/EISA system I/O.

o  Scalablity -- Two CPUs are included, providing an effective symmetric
   multiprocessing environment; up to four CPUs are available to meet your
   growing needs

o  Optimization tools -- You optimize application performance and design,
   gaining a competitive advantage.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital 2100 A500TDS Technical Developer's System will be available in
the second quarter this year through the Early Ship Program with DEC OSF/1
V3.0 and field test layered products. Final releases of field test products
will be provided when available.

