AdvantageCluster Compute Servers 1000, 2000, 3000, and 4000

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Alpha AXP Packaged Farms (formerly Digital Cluster Parallel Systems) have
   new family name: AdvantageCluster Compute Servers

o  The packages enhanced with additional prepackaged software tools for
   application development, application tuning, overall cluster management

o  Each system in AdvantageCluster Compute Servers, including all custom
   configurations, configured, quoted, priced under single order number

o  Digital now provides the most productive and innovative compute servers,
   complete with hardware and software for technical computing

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

High performance networked systems based on workstation technology (commonly
called "workstation farms" or "UNIX clusters") are very attractive as low
cost servers and even as alternatives to mainframes and supercomputers for
compute intensive applications.

Digital is now offering four packaged systems tailored to meet your needs
for systems that are easy to configure, install, and use, easily scalable to
incorporate new technology and add computing power, and easily integrated
with other UNIX systems. They provide higher throughput for your existing
applications and constitute a powerful platform for developing parallel
applications.

All four systems are based on Alpha AXP technology and the DEC OSF/1
operating system and all are rackmounted in a standard Digital enclosure. In
addition, Digital offers Ethernet or GIGAswitch interconnects. The
GIGAswitch product is an intelligent, high speed communications switch that
employs multiple dynamic FDDI links to achieve unprecedented throughput and
connectivity. It is open (connecting to any DEC 3000 system and to any
vendor's FDDI system and allowing for heterogeneous systems networking) and
ATM-ready, can be managed easily by SNMP based software, and provides a
smooth migration to future switch technologies.

For a complete hardware description of the AdvantageCluster Compute Server
1000, 2000, and 3000 systems, see the "DEC 3000 Model 600 AXP and 800 AXP
Workstations" article in the October 25, 1993, issue of Digital's Customer
Update (AXP FARM 1000, 2000, and 3000). For a complete hardware description
of the AdvantageCluster Compute Server 4000 system, see the "Digital Cluster
Parallel System 4000" article in the February 14, 1994, issue.

Digital has also greatly enhanced its existing popular packaged systems by
including an extensive suite of powerful software tools for batch and
parallel processing, application development, application tuning, and
overall network management. These tools (all factory installed) include:

o  LSF (Load Sharing Facility) cluster software.
o  PVM (Parallel Virtual Machine).
o  DXML (Digital Extended Math Library).
o  POLYCENTER Console Manager.
o  POLYCENTER FullSail.
o  POLYCENTER Advanced File System.
o  POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore.
o  DEC Fortran 90.
o  Parallel Software Environment.
o  C++.
o  Fortran 77.
o  DEC FUSE software.
o  KAP Fortran and C preprocessor.
o  DEC OSF Developer's Extension V1.2.

BENEFITS

With the AdvantageCluster Compute Server family of hardware and software
products, users who may not be experts on workstation farm technology and
the various software tools now have an easy way to configure a system. The
completely packaged systems eliminate the need for extensive cabling and
hardware/software assembly. Each solution is unique to your needs, but the
packaging method ensures that the solution begins with a tested, workable
core. The innovative software tools included in the packages enable you not
only to develop and tune code but also to manage the execution of workloads
across very powerful clusters. Furthermore, you can grow your systems over
time through optional systems and software as computing needs increase.

The overall benefit of the product family is the combination of high
performance with a low price, exceptional scalability, and significantly
improved productivity. The compute servers can run any of your applications,
whether electronic CAD or computational fluid dynamics (CFD) or other
complex software. The turnaround time on a mix of batch jobs (a common use
of large compute servers) is greatly improved, because of the powerful
aggregrate batch processing power of the AdvantageCluster Compute Servers.
In addition, they can act as a powerful, multipurpose parallel processing
system, letting you develop parallel programs and solve problems that once
were not within your reach.

Thus the AdvantageCluster family represents a solid investment in systems
that are open, extensible, and modular in design, offering not only an
excellent platform for batch and parallel processing today but a very
promising grow path to the future.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

