VAX 4000 Model 105A and ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Performance rich (150 TPS TPC-A estimated) desktop systems boost
   performance by 33 percent for same price as VAX 4000 Model 100A

o  Connection to HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI converter allows expanded support for
   SCSI devices via DSSI bus, while maintaining all benefits of DSSI
   clusters, including dual-host access

o  Support for industry's best clustering technology positions new system as
   perfect upgrade path to Digital 2100 Server with any combination of mixed
   Alpha AXP and VAX OpenVMS clusters via DSSI

o  ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES to new system preserve your investment in your
   installed systems; enhanced packaging makes ordering VAX 4000 product
   family much easier

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new VAX 4000 Model 105A desktop system is a quality driven, performance
rich solution. It joins a family of VAX systems that are well integrated and
run over 10,000 OpenVMS applications. In addition, it offers a direct line
into the next generation of Alpha AXP systems: the Digital 2100 series.
Space saving rackmountable versions with the same features are also
available.

The VAX 4000 Model 105A combines the power of the NVAX CMOS-4 processor, the
richness of DSSI and DSSI VMScluster systems, the maturity of the OpenVMS
operating system, and the ease of Q-bus connectivity with low cost memory,
power, and packaging designs. It includes:

o  A faster CPU based on the NVAX chip running at 12 ns.
o  A cache size of 512 Kbytes, four times that of the Model 100A.
o  External connection to the HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI converter to access a
   variety of disks and tapes in open StorageWorks configurations (the HSD05
   StorageWorks DSSI-to-SCSI expansion product is supported via the system
   DSSI buses).
o  Support for DSSI VMScluster systems.
o  Support of OpenVMS V5.5-2H4 and V6.1 (V6.0 is not supported).
o  Coexistence with Alpha AXP based systems via DECnet transports over the
   Ethernet, plus tight coupling with VAX and Alpha AXP VMScluster systems
   over the DSSI channel.
o  Support for base systems, packaged systems, and upgrades.
o  Support for the BA42B tabletop enclosure (the MicroVAX 3100 family
   enclosure), with cable connections for Q-bus connectivity (a separate
   enclosure is required to use the Q-bus backplane).

With the 12 ns NVAX chip, the new system can achieve up to 150 transactions
per second (TPS) for commercial applications. It delivers processing power
at 32 VUPs, so technical applications can benefit from datacenter-like
performance for their desktop and workgroup computing needs.

One of the best ways to achieve the highest levels of system performance,
availability, and expansion is through DSSI VMScluster technology. When
Q-bus VAX 4000 systems are joined via DSSI, each system in the cluster can
access and share all disks attached to the DSSI buses, providing multiple
paths to data. By connecting your new desktop to an HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI
converter via the DSSI bus, you can greatly expand its SCSI disk capacity
and enhance your open StorageWorks solutions. Continued support of the Q-bus
for expansion and compatibility with existing options and DSSI makes the
Model 105A a very attractive upgrade choice for Q-bus MicroVAX 3000 series
or VAX 4200 machines.

Model 105A ADVANTAGE-SERVER systems have been packaged to include NAS 200
and Motif. NAS 200, the popular choice of many users, includes DECnet and
TCP/IP transports, a PATHWORKS server, and the POLYCENTER Software
Distribution client.

The VAX 4105A offers the future built-in. Planned VAX and Alpha AXP
coexistence makes it possible for clustered systems to share the same
software, data, applications, networks, clusters, and peripherals. Whether
you are upgrading from a MicroVAX system or are ready to move to a Digital
2100 system, ADVANTAGE-SERVER systems will provide the strongest backbone
possible for open, client/server networks and downsized environments.

ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES

ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE paths to the VAX 4000 Model 105A will preserve your
investment in your installed systems while you upgrade system performance.
ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE paths from the following systems are available:
VAX-11/780; MicroVAX II, MicroVAX 3300, 3400, 3500, 3800, and 3900; and VAX
4000 Models 100, 100A, and 200. These ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES are the most
cost-effective methods to achieve the performance and other benefits of the
VAX 4000 Model 105A.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The new VAX 4000 Model 105A desktop system is available now. It supports
OpenVMS V5.5-2H4 and V6.1; if you have V6.0, you will need to upgrade to
V6.1. The ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES are governed by standard terms and conditions.

