TechAdvantage Software for DEC OSF/1 AXP Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  TechAdvantage software family will contain innovative technical software
   development solutions from Digital

o  Developers will be able to order all the technical application
   development tools they need from Digital in one package

o  Initial packages will provide Fortran 90, Fortran 77, and C++ solutions

PRODUCT OVERVIEW

Digital's new TechAdvantage family of technical software products will
consist of innovative technical software and include complete packages for
technical application developers. You will be able to look to this family
for leadership technical software solutions.

Accompanying articles in this issue are highlighting the following new
individual TechAdvantage software products for technical computing:

o  DEC Fortran 90 V1.0, a compiler for the new Fortran 90 language standard.
   It produces code for parallel Alpha AXP farms and SMP systems as well as
   for scalar workstations and servers.

o  Digital Parallel Software Environment (PSE) V1.0. This is the execution
   environment and tools that support DEC Fortran 90 for parallel
   application deployment.

o  LSF V1.2 (Load Sharing Facility). This third party software sold by
   Digital automatically distributes jobs to the least loaded system in a
   UNIX network.

Also included in the TechAdvantage family are the following previously
announced products: DEC C++, DEC Fortran compilers, the C Developer's
Extensions Toolkit, the Digital Extended Math Library (DXML), KAP third
party software, and the DEC FUSE and DEC FUSE for C++ products.

TechAdvantage SOFTWARE PACKAGES PROGRAM ANNOUNCEMENT

Digital is planning TechAdvantage software packages that will take the
confusion and risk out of acquiring the proper suite of technical software
development tools. There will be a series of developer's kits for Fortran
90, Fortran 77, and C++ developers. The Fortran packages will contain the
software tools to facilitate porting and optimization of applications for
scalar as well as parallel execution. In addition, Digital is planning to
include a CD containing the various free software that developers need, such
as GNU tools, multimedia tools, demos, and PVM (Parallel Virtual Machine)
software.

The packages will contain the following materials (contents may change prior
to final product announcement):

o  TechAdvantage High Performance Fortran 90 package: DEC Fortran 90
   compiler, Digital Parallel Software Environment, LSF, C Developer's
   Extension, and complete documentation -- plus media containing popular
   free software.

o  TechAdvantage Fortran 77 package: DEC Fortran, KAP, PVM, DXML, DEC FUSE,
   LSF, C Developer's Extension, and complete documentation -- plus media
   containing popular free software.

o  TechAdvantage C++ package: DEC C, DEC C++, KAP, PVM, DXML, DEC FUSE, DEC
   FUSE for C++, LSF, C Developer's Extension, and complete documentation --
   plus media containing popular free software.

o  TechAdvantage free software CD package: GNU tools, multimedia tools,
   demos, PVM, and other products.

BENEFITS

o  Technical users can look to Digital's TechAdvantage family for innovative
   technical products and solutions.

o  Developers can use one order number to receive all the software tools
   needed to work in Fortran 90, Fortran 77, or C++.

o  TechAdvantage software, along with DEC OSF/1 AXP systems, gives you a
   winning technical advantage.

