Digital Parallel Software Environment for DEC OSF/1 AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Parallel Software Environment consists of execution environment and
   parallel tools that support development, tuning, and deployment of
   parallel Fortran 90 applications for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems

o  DEC Fortran 90 compiler, which supports High Performance Fortran (HPF)
   extensions, can compile programs to run on parallel Alpha AXP systems,
   such as Alpha AXP Farms and DEC OSF/1 AXP SMP systems

o  Reduced pricing available for limited time

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

To write parallel programs in Fortran, programmers will prefer using the new
DEC Fortran 90 compiler (see the accompanying article in this issue), which
includes the High Performance Fortran (HPF) extensions. These extensions
enable programmers to express their requirements in a convenient form
without using explicit message passing, independently of any particular
DEC OSF/1 AXP platform.

To allow for execution and debugging of parallel DEC Fortran 90 applications
on Alpha AXP systems, Digital is introducing the Digital Parallel Software
Environment (PSE). This software contains a parallel profiler and the system
software, which is composed of an execution environment and several
utilities. The Digital Parallel Software Environment, in combination with
the DEC Fortran 90 compiler, will allow programmers to quickly develop
parallel programs on a single workstation and then recompile and execute on
parallel Alpha AXP systems.

The Parallel Software Environment components are as follows:

o  The profiler allows users and programmers to view how programs execute in
   parallel. This is important in locating hot spots and program
   bottlenecks, identifying interprocessor communications and costs, and
   learning the impact of data distribution techniques. With this data,
   programmers can return to the program and make changes that will speed
   parallel execution.

o  The parallel environment is defined in a database that describes the
   configuration by using a Domain Name System. Features include
   partitioning of groups of machines, access control, communication option
   definition, and scheduling priority. Commands for database configuration
   are included.

o  Commands and facilities, including a daemon process, allow users to start
   and stop jobs across a partition, kill a job, establish and configure a
   partition, and view the status of processes across the partition. If you
   have the Load Sharing Facility (LSF) installed, jobs can also be
   submitted to the LSF to optimize the utilization of resources on an Alpha
   AXP farm.

o  The transparent message passing facility optimizes interprocessor
   communications for speed and efficiency via a fastpath through socket and
   protocol layers. The message passing facility already supports TCP/IP and
   therefore will accommodate new communications technologies such as ATM.

The Digital High Performance Fortran 90 package is being offered to help
scalar DEC Fortran 90 users experiment with parallel DEC Fortran 90. This
package includes a single Concurrent Use DEC Fortran 90 compiler license, a
tiered capacity Digital Parallel Software Environment license, and
documentation kits for both products. This package costs only a little more
than the DEC Fortran 90 license alone and it contains everything needed to
compile and execute parallel programs on a single node Alpha AXP system.

BENEFITS

o  When you use the Digital Parallel Software Environment and DEC Fortran 90
   to create High Performance Fortran 90 programs, you will typically
   experience faster runtimes when programs are executed on parallel DEC
   OSF/1 AXP systems.

o  Programs created using DEC Fortran 90 are easier to maintain and modify
   than programs written using Fortran 77 with explicit message passing.
   Changes in the data decomposition mode do not mean a program rewrite with
   DEC Fortran 90.

o  Development and debugging of applications can be done on parallel Alpha
   AXP systems, where development time is often more affordable than on
   supercomputers. If necessary, the same application can then be executed
   on a supercomputer after initial development is completed.

o  Independent application suppliers will adopt DEC Fortran 90, to develop
   and maintain parallel versions of their applications more easily (the
   applications are intended to run in a variety of execution environments).

o  If you have a supercomputer, you can easily downsize some supercomputer
   applications to parallel Alpha AXP systems, freeing the supercomputer to
   work on the very large projects it does best.

o  If you choose not to invest in a supercomputer, you can achieve
   additional application performance by running DEC Fortran 90 applications
   on parallel Alpha AXP systems.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital Parallel Software Environment for DEC OSF/1 AXP software will be
shipping in August 1994. It will be available for a limited time at a
reduced price. Software loans are also available.

The Digital Parallel Software Environment for DEC OSF/1 AXP will be included
on the Consolidated Distribution CDROM and the documentation will be on the
Online Documentation CDROM.

Order one DEC Fortran 90 license for each system that will be used for
compilation. Typically, only one is needed. Order a Digital Parallel
Software Environment license for each system that will be a part of the
parallel execution environment.

