InfoBroker Server for OSF/1 AXP and Client for Windows

HIGHLIGHTS

o  InfoBroker harnesses growing amounts of scattered information, making it
   easy to locate, access, and manage this information at workgroup level

o  Infobroker ensures easy, cost-effective growth path to enterprise X.500
   directory service through standards based format

o  InfoBroker starter kit, providing everything you need to get started
   today, available at special introductory price for limited time

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Directory services, for both corporate information services and common
network resource naming, are considered key components in helping users and
network managers deal with the increasingly complex computing world of
distributed users, systems, applications, and data.

Major systems vendors and standards organizations are pointing toward the
use of a common directory specification, such as CCITT X.500, as a way to
allow multivendor networks, applications, and their users to coexist more
easily.

Digital's InfoBroker Server V1.0 for OSF/1 AXP (SPD 53.32) and InfoBroker
Client V1.0 for Microsoft Windows (SPD 53.33) collectively enable network
adminstrators and end users to locate, access, and manage information about
network users, network resources, documents, and applications.

Administrator or developer customization of the InfoBroker server brings an
unlimited number of possible usages and types of information to be stored,
such as database or application names and locations. Likewise, customizable
display screens can be created with the InfoBroker client to reflect your
specific implementation of the InfoBroker server.

InfoBroker Server V1.0 for OSF/1 AXP is an X.500 based workgroup directory
with a gateway capability for direct access to X.500 directories. When
configured as a local directory, the InfoBroker server contains information
such as user name, phone number, mail address, FAX number, and photos.
Information can be added easily using text editors and other simple tools.

Information is stored in this local directory in a standards based X.500
format, so it can be loaded easily into an enterprise-wide X.500 directory
service. You can deploy multiple, independent workgroup directories in
conjunction with your advanced, corporate-wide X.500 planning, thus
significantly enhancing your ability to create a smooth growth path to a
corporate-wide X.500 directory service.

Additionally, the InfoBroker server can act as a gateway for InfoBroker
client access to an already existing X.500 directory service.

InfoBroker Client V1.0 for Microsoft Windows is an easy-to-use, Windows
based PC application that lets you access, browse, and search for
information in the InfoBroker server or in an X.500 directory server via the
InfoBroker server. The InfoBroker client can also be used with Digital's
MAILworks Server for OSF/1 product, which includes the InfoBroker server and
its related functionality.

The InfoBroker client features such capabilities as a default search window
for information about people, a graphical user interface based utility for
creating and customizing search windows, online hypertext help, and the
ability to display photos.

Additionally, the InfoBroker client provides you with administration tools,
such as a loading and populating tool, which enables an administrator to
extract information easily from cc:Mail and Microsoft Mail post offices and
then populate the InfoBroker server.

InfoBroker uses industry standard TCP/IP or DECnet transport protocols to
communicate via the Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP). Support of
this standard protocol allows for easy integration into LDAP compliant
client/server environments.

BENEFITS

o  Locating information about fellow employees, such as phone numbers or
   mail addresses, is difficult and time consuming -- but the InfoBroker
   client provides a simple, accurate, and timely way to access this
   information via a Windows based application.

o  Setting up a large corporate X.500 directory service is a complex task --
   but the InfoBroker server provides a workgroup level, X.500 based flat
   file directory with load tools for buildup and incorporation into a
   corporate X.500 directory.

o  Product development groups require an easy method to find information or
   documentation about other products and/or corporate product development
   guidelines -- The administrator can easily customize the InfoBroker
   server and create a directory file structure for product data and related
   attributes.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

