BASEstar Open

BASEstar Open utilizes standard client/server technology and architecture
components, allowing integration in a true multivendor environment.
BASEstar Open components are based on industry standards, reinforcing
Digital's commitment and leadership on open systems. BASEstar Open supports
the implementation of high availability configurations in heterogeneous
environments.

DECosap

DECosap supports the connection of BASEstar (and other) integration
platforms with processors providing Siemens communication services. This
includes services such as environmental management, virtual manufacturing
device support, variable access, serial transfer,  program invocation,
domain services, and message exchanging.

Digital's Open Advantage for Device Interconnect

High efficiency manufacturing operations require the availability of
cost-effective, reliable, and easy-to-use communication channels connecting
plant floor equipment to host computers.

BASEstar Open provides this capability by using DEComni as the common device
interconnect API based on the standard MMS model (ISO 9506). Specific
communication services are developed below the DEComni API; control vendors'
devices, when supported, are accessible through it. The announced Device
Access Software provides a method to communicate with Allen-Bradley and
Modicon plant floor equipment. The support covers the OSF/1 AXP and OpenVMS
VAX operating systems.

