TeamLinks for Macintosh V2.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  TeamLinks Mail, Routing, and Office for Macintosh V2.0 products, program
   announced in 1993, to ship by April 30, 1994

o  Enhanced TeamLinks Mail integration with ALL-IN-1 IOS server

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The TeamLinks for Macintosh V2.0 products deliver the same capabilities as
the TeamLinks for Windows products currently shipping. These include the
option to select ALL-IN-1 IOS or DEC MAILworks software as your mail server.
Associated with this option is support for ALL-IN-1 IOS mail addressing and
validation, document reservation, better file cabinet support, and remote
access.

For TeamLinks users using either the DEC MAILworks server or the ALL-IN-1
IOS server, TeamLinks V2.0 includes significant improvements in user
interface and ease of use and new features to support remote and portable
drawers and easier mobile computing.

TeamLinks software complies with key standards (such as X.400) and offers a
scalable deployment that can support users ranging from small workgroups to
enterprises with over 100,000 people.

For further product information please consult TeamLinks Mail for Macintosh
SPD 39.62, TeamLinks Routing for Macintosh SPD 46.26, and TeamLinks Office
for Macintosh SPD 48.17.

BENEFITS

o  If you are an ALL-IN-1 IOS user, you can move your Macintosh systems to
   TeamLinks clients while keeping IOS as your mail and file server. Thus
   there is no need to install a second mail server (the DEC MAILworks
   server).

o  Without retraining, the ALL-IN-1 and TeamLinks user can use such familiar
   services as system distribution lists, nicknames, directory services,
   address validation, auto-reply, and auto-forward.

o  IS managers can be flexible in choosing network connection protocols. The
   TeamLinks user can connect to the DEC MAILworks server or ALL-IN-1 IOS
   server, using the DECnet and PATHWORKS, AppleTalk (with  an AppleTalk
   DECnet gateway), Remote AppleTalk for asynchronous connection (with an
   AppleTalk DECnet gateway), or TCP/IP protocols.

