tools currently supported on Windows, Windows NT, DEC OSF/1, and OpenVMS
systems. On any of these platforms, PATHWORKS SDK V5.1 allows application
developers to select from a list of open, standard distributed application
interfaces, including OMG CORBA and OSF DCE.

The PATHWORKS SDK supports multivendor queueing by integrating DECMessageQ
software into the product capabilities. InfoBroker and its Local Data Access
Protocol (LDAP) API provide an enterprise-wide search capability through a
callable interface. The PATHWORKS SDK augments ManageWORKS -- Digital's new,
powerful, PC based multivendor system and network management application --
with a set of APIs that enable application developers to build tailored
resource management applications that run within a ManageWORKS framework.
The PATHWORKS SDK is intended for developers of these applications whether
they choose to develop from their PC or in their existing server operating
system environment.

The kit features online help, tutorials, sample programs, and illustrative
demos. Since the tools are available on the most popular platforms, you can
easily achieve application integration with other major development
environments that span multiple network operating systems.

The kit offers a complete set of middleware tools for developing new
applications and updating legacy applications to run across multivendor
networks. With the inclusion of Digital's object-oriented tools (which will
be integrated with Microsoft's Object Linking and Embedding technology), you
can develop shrinkwrapped networked applications tomorrow.

BENEFITS

Because you require a consistent set of APIs for building applications that
run over multiple platforms, and because developers often adopt a variety of
programming styles, Digital has brought together a rich set of features and
benefits:

o  ManageWORKS APIs enable developers to write client/server applications
   that can be easily managed from their PCs. This application allows
   administrators to view and manage essential aspects of a client/server
   network directly from a remote PC through a single, advanced graphical
   user interface. Moreover, ManageWORKS reduces the administrative time and
   costs associated with system management, while providing improved asset
   management and control. The unique, PC based nature of ManageWORKS
   provides PC server and network operating system independence -- unlike
   many competing solutions.

o  ObjectBroker is Digital's object request broker, complying with the
   Object Management Group's CORBA specification, the standard for central
   communication and integration of software objects. OMG CORBA is
   middleware software technology that is specifically designed to help you
   integrate existing legacy applications with new applications, extend
   existing applications to new hardware platforms, and integrate products
   within dynamic framework environments. It provides distributed object
   technology that enables developers to write applications more
   efficiently.

o  The Digital Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) product set provides
   an interoperable set of the distributed computing functionality specified
   for the Open Software Foundation's DCE, as well as tools for application
   developers. With DCE, OSF has established a standard set of services and
   interfaces that facilitate the creation, use, and maintenance of
   client/server applications. Digital DCE serves as the basis for an open
   computing environment where networks of multivendor systems appear as a
   single system to the user. Since DCE makes the underlying networks and
   operating systems transparent, application developers can easily build
   portable, interoperable applications. Users can locate and share
   information safely and easily across the entire enterprise. Digital's DCE
   offers a consistent model for the naming and security needs of
   applications that are deployed across heterogeneous systems.

o  Digital's InfoBroker Server for OSF/1 AXP and InfoBroker Client for
   Microsoft Windows collectively provide network adminstrators and end
   users with the ability to manage, control, and access information about
   network users, network resources, documents, and applications. PATHWORKS
   SDK V5.1 provides developers with a callable interface to the InfoBroker
   client and server Local Data Access Protocol API.

o  The DECmessageQ product provides a powerful, yet easy-to-use set of tools
   for building distributed software solutions for heterogenous, multivendor
   distributed computing environments. It features message recovery
   services, selective broadcast services, productivity tools, and
   integration features that allow for efficient and effective development
   of distributed applications. It supports both asynchronous and
   synchronous client/server interprocess application models and is
   currently used in many mission critical applications.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

PATHWORKS Software Developers' Kit (SDK) V5.1 will be made available between
June and August 1994 on the Windows, Windows NT (Intel and AXP), DEC OSF/1,
and OpenVMS (VAX and AXP) platforms.

