VAXcluster and VMScluster Software for OpenVMS V6.1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Your choice of cluster solution is now architecture independent:
   Digital's industry leading VAXcluster and VMScluster systems are now
   functionally equivalent

o  Support for the KFMSB adapter means that VAX 7000 and VAX 10000 systems
   using DSSI as their cluster interconnect can now be upgraded to DEC 7000
   AXP and DEC 10000 AXP systems

o  FDDI support is now available on all Alpha AXP systems and a wide range
   of VAX systems

o  System management of VAXcluster and VMScluster systems is enhanced
   through inclusion of the DEC Availability Manager for Distributed Systems
   (DECamds) in the VAXcluster and VMScluster software products

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

With the release of VAXcluster Software for OpenVMS VAX V6.1 (SPD 29.78.08)
and VMScluster Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1 (SPD 42.18.01), you can now
acquire affordable systems that offer high availability, leadership
performance, and easy system management. The new features and benefits
offered by these two products can be summarized as follows:

o  DEC Availability Manager for Distributed Systems -- DECamds features have
   been included in both cluster products, so users with a license for
   either VAXcluster or VMScluster software now have the right to the
   DECamds functionality.

   This functionality includes realtime monitoring, investigation,
   diagnosing, and correction capabilities. The driver portion runs in each
   node being monitored and directs its output to a centralized display.
   System level data can be analyzed at the display station, with corrective
   action proposed. Refer to the article in the March 14, 1994, issue of
   Digital's Customer Update for more information.

o  Cross-Architecture Satellite Booting -- Both software products provide
   support for performing cross-architecture satellite booting. This permits
   VAX boot nodes to provide boot service to AXP satellites, and AXP boot
   nodes to provide boot service to VAX satellites. This feature reduces the
   entry cost of adding Alpha AXP systems in existing VAXcluster systems.

o  Virtual I/O Cache -- V6.1 of OpenVMS AXP software supports virtual I/O
   caching. This enables portions of processor memory to be dynamically
   allocated to caching data read from storage devices. This is especially
   good for read-only files, such as images, and decreases the amount of
   system I/O bandwidth required.

o  TMSCP Server -- The TMSCP (Tape Mass Storage Control Protocol) server is
   now supported in Alpha AXP systems running the OpenVMS AXP operating
   system. All TMSCP compatible tapes locally connected to an AXP node are
   now available to all members of the VMScluster system, increasing
   resource sharing in these systems.

o  Increased System Support -- VMScluster Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1 has
   been qualified to support more large systems in a VMScluster system: it
   supports any combination of up to 16 DEC 4000 AXP, DEC 7000 AXP, or DEC
   10000 AXP systems. You can benefit significantly from the large increase
   in processing power thus available in a VMScluster configuration. The new
   limits equal those for similar VAX systems. The number of CIXCD adapters
   supported in a VMScluster system has been increased to 10.

o  Enhanced Adapter Support -- VMScluster Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1
   supports the KFMSB adapter. Alpha-ready VAX 7000 and VAX 10000 systems
   using the DSSI as their cluster interconnect can now be upgraded to DEC
   7000 AXP and DEC 10000 AXP systems.

   This software also supports the DEFEA (EISA to FDDI) adapter, while
   VAXcluster Software for OpenVMS VAX V6.1 supports the new DEFQA (FDDI to
   Q-bus) and DEFTA (FDDI to TURBOchannel) adapters. This new support brings
   the benefits of FDDI, such as high bandwidth and clustering over a 40
   kilometer distance, to more VAX and AXP systems.

   Summarizing the new adapter support:

   New Adapter      Functionality           Systems Benefited

   KFMSB	    XMI to DSSI		    DEC 7000/10000 AXP
   DEFQA	    Q-bus to FDDI	    VAX 3000/4000; DEC 3000/4000 AXP
   DEFTA	    TURBOchannel to FDDI    DEC 3000 AXP; VAX 4000-90
   DEFEA	    EISA to FDDI	    DEC 2000 AXP

o  New System Services -- Three new system services have been added to
   VMScluster Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1. They provide for automatic
   notification when a node leaves or enters a VMScluster system. This
   feature enhances the performance of database systems, such as Rdb. For
   more information, refer to the systems services manual in the OpenVMS
   documentation set.

o  Mixed-Architecture VMScluster Systems -- These versions of VAXcluster and
   VMScluster software have been qualified for coexistence in
   mixed-architecture VMScluster systems. These versions can also run with
   other versions of VAXcluster software (back to V5.5-2) and VMScluster
   software (back to V1.5). Consult SPD 29.78.08 for specifics.

o  Volume Shadowing as System Integrated Product -- Volume shadowing will be
   distributed as a system integrated product beginning with OpenVMS AXP
   V6.1. This will simplify the distribution and installation of a product
   commonly used in VMScluster systems.

o  Functional Equivalence and Industry Leadership -- These releases of
   cluster software make VAXcluster and VMScluster systems functionally
   equivalent. You now have an architecturally independent choice for your
   cluster solution from Digital, including more configuration choices,
   better system management capabilities, and increased performance.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

VAXcluster Software for OpenVMS VAX V6.1 will be available at the end of
this month. VMScluster Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1 will be available in
May.

