Rackmountable VAX 4000 Model 105A and ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES

HIGHLIGHTS

o  VAX 4000 Model 105A rackmount systems provide latest technology in
   space saving, industry standard EIA-RS-210 racks or cabinets

o  ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES to rackmount configurations offer paths from
   VAX-11/780, MicroVAX II, MicroVAX 3300, 3400, 3500, 3800, and 3900, and
   VAX 4000 Models 100/100A and 200 in BA2xx and BA4xx enclosures

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The rackmountable VAX 4000 Model 105A systems are mechanically reconfigured
VAX 4000 Model 105A systems. The same configurations available as desktops
-- base, timeshare, preconfigured, dual host, and ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE -- are
available in the rackmountable versions. The functionality is also the same:
mass storage, media, memory, power, external Q-bus, SCSI, and DSSI ports,
and other capabilities.

The rackmountable VAX 4000 Model 105A system is mounted sideways on a
slide-shelf assembly that occupies 8.75 inches of vertical rack space and
has front-to-rear cooling to permit close stacking of units, saving valuable
space. The slide-shelf allows for easy, left-side access to the removable
storage locations and for service access. Two external Q-bus ports and two
external DSSI ports have been relocated to the top cover for cable
management reasons. A cabinet is not included under the model order number,
but cabinets of all types and sizes are available to meet your needs.

