New Class of TZ87 Tape Drive and TZ877 Tape Subsystem

HIGHLIGHTS

o  The TZ87N drives and TZ877 autoloaders provide the same capacity and
   performance as Digital's industry leading TZ87 DLT tape drives -- at a
   significantly lower cost

o  They are ideal for backup, archiving, and some data interchange
   applications for users with compact discs, 9 track drives, or other
   TK/DLT drives as load mechanisms for their Digital software

o  They differ from earlier members of the DLT family in only one respect:
   they do not read TK media

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is introducing a new class of DLT (digital linear tape) drive, the
TZ87N, for users who do not require TK50 or TK70 compatibility. The TZ87N
DLT tape drive and its companion, the TZ877-NE/NF autoloader, provide the
capacity, performance, reliability, and system support that you expect from
a DLT drive -- and at a lower price. They are compatible with media written
by other DLT tape drives and loaders, including the Tx85, Tx86, and Tx87
drives and autoloaders, and are ideal high performance, unattended backup
solutions for OpenVMS (VAX and AXP) and ULTRIX systems and NetWare LANs.

If you have VAX or AXP systems that use either system or InfoServer based
CDROM drives, TK compatible members of the DLT tape drive family, or 9 track
tape for software loading, you can use the TZ87N and TZ877-NE/NF product
set. If you require load software, you will need compact disc, 9 track, or
other TK/DLT software load mechanisms for your Digital software. If you rely
on TK based media for data interchange or your own software distribution,
you should review your requirements carefully before purchasing a
TZ87N based product.

For related product information, please see the "TZ87 and TZ877 Digital
Linear Tape Systems" article in the December 20, 1993, issue of Digital's
Customer Update and the "TZ87/TZ877 Additional Support and New Variants"
article in the March 14, 1994, issue.

BENEFITS

The lower priced, TZ87N based products offer leadership performance,
capacity, and reliability:

o  Their backup rate of up to 9 Gbytes per hour ensures that most backup
   jobs can be completed within the brief periods typically available for
   backup.

o  A per-cartridge backup capacity of up to 20 Gbytes and a per-loader
   backup capacity of 140 Gbytes provide the unattended capacity required
   for even very large backup jobs.

o  The advanced linear tape path of TZ87N drives increases their useful life
   by up to five times that of 8 mm drives, while eliminating head wear-out.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TZ87N DLT tape drive and TZ877-NE/NF autoloader are available now.

