KAP Update

IN THIS SECTION:

o  KAP Support for Windows NT Program Announcement

o  KAP to Support Parallel Programming for DEC OSF/1 AXP

KAP SUPPORT FOR Windows NT PROGRAM ANNOUNCEMENT

The combination of Digital's Alpha AXP platform, with its impressive
computational performance, and Microsoft's Windows NT operating system, with
its ease of use and powerful features, is attracting users away from
traditional engineering workstations.

To help provide end users and developers with the same high quality language
products they have been accustomed to on their workstations, Digital is
extending its KAP language preprocessor offering to support Alpha AXP
systems running Windows NT. KAP for Windows NT will provide a set of
powerful program analysis, inlining, and optimization features to improve
program performance and programmer productivity.

V1.0 will be available this summer, with versions for both Fortran and C.

KAP TO SUPPORT PARALLEL PROGRAMMING FOR DEC OSF/1 AXP

Users with compute intensive codes that would benefit from the additional
processors on an SMP system need a way to decompose their codes to run
across the processors. Digital is extending its KAP language preprocessor
offering to support parallel decomposition of Fortran and C programs.

KAP V2.0 will provide both automatic and directed decomposition of programs.
(Automatic decomposition means that there is no need to modify a program or
rewrite it in another language. Thus it makes an SMP solution painless and
effective.) The KAP automatic decomposition feature will analyze an existing
program to locate loops that are candidates for parallel execution and will
then decompose the loops and insert all necessary synchronization points. If
more control is desired, the programmer can manually insert directives to
control the parallelization of individual loops. In addition, a new set of
optimizations will be enabled when the parallelization option is selected.
These optimizations will attempt to increase the amount of potential
parallelism and remove impediments to parallelization.

KAP will still perform all its usual serial code optimizations, including:

o  Advanced memory management.
o  Data blocking.
o  Complete suite of loop transformations.
o  Extensive support of inlining.
o  Annotated program listings (Fortran only).

Please keep in mind that while the decomposition support represents
additional value for your systems, not every program will benefit from
parallelization.

Note also that the KAP parallelization technology is a tested and mature
technology that has been deployed on various systems for five years. It is
available for both Fortran 77 and C, the most popular languages used for
compute intensive applications.

The DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.0 release will support parallelization of both Fortran
and C programs, using a threads interface for improved efficiency. (The
current DEC OSF/1 AXP release is V1.5.)

The DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.0 release with SMP support will be available in August.
The OpenVMS AXP V2.0 release is available now for Fortran decomposition
support.

