DEC ACB (AUTOMATIC CALL BACK) FOR OpenVMS V2.1

DEC ACB for OpenVMS V2.1 is a general purpose security package with
security, authentication, and management features. As a management utility,
it facilitates secure connection to an OpenVMS VAX system from a terminal or
PC.

You can access a host system running DEC ACB directly or you can supply a
telephone number, whereupon DEC ACB will call you back and start the
required session. You can be validated by the local DEC ACB system or on a
remote DEC ACB system running the Remote Authentication Interface Server (an
option available in a DECnet network).

Each user is authenticated on the basis of a random challenge and response,
which protects the system from Replay Attacks. The password is automatically
changed at each connection, creating a secure system that requires minimal
password management and that renders line tapping ineffective. Use of the
Racal Watchword Generator is included, and any other type of
challenge/response system can be integrated easily into a DEC ACB system.

DEC ACB supports access from PCs running MS-DOS and MS-Windows. The PC
clients contain simple user interfaces that allow you to automate the
connection sequence and connect to the host system (after authentication)
from local or remote locations.

The Reporting and Billing utility reports usage of the DEC ACB system, using
user-definable fields in the accounting file to calculate operating costs
based on local PSDN charges and currencies.

A DEC ACB system can be managed remotely, saving operating costs, and can
optionally report security and operational related events to DECmcc
software.

Other product features:

o  DEC ACB is a component of Digital's POLYCENTER solution.
o  It provides an application programming interface that allows:
   - Modem driver development.
   - Authentication development.
   - Database and accounting information storage and retrieval.
   - User validation (using authentication).

DEC ACB for OpenVMS V2.1 is available now, offering traditional and
concurrent use licenses. The DEC ACB PC client offers personal use and
unlimited system use licenses.

