DEC DISK STRIPING FOR OpenVMS AXP V1.5

With DEC Disk Striping for OpenVMS AXP V1.5 (SPD 53.26.00), you can now
obtain Alpha AXP performance for:

o  Applications that require very high data transfer rates or systems in
   which static disk load balancing is ineffective.

o  Applications that are prohibited from distributing data across multiple
   disks but need a throughput higher than that available from a single
   disk.

Disk striping interleaves multiple disks to improve I/O performance in the
same way that high performance memory systems interleave memory banks. In
each case, data requests are decomposed and distributed to physical storage
components that process those requests in parallel.

The DEC Disk Striping product lets you create one or more stripesets, each
composed of two or more physical disk drives and represented to the user
application (and operating system) as a single pseudo-device. Stripesets
must be composed of disks of a single type.

A Digital Command Language (DCL) interface (CLI) is provided to enable the
privileged user to define stripesets and to create and destroy the pseudo-
devices that represent them. It also allows statistics and configuration
information associated with the pseudo-devices to be listed.

Please note that DEC Disk Striping for OpenVMS AXP V1.5 does not support
MSCP serving of stripesets to other nodes in a VMScluster system. The
equivalent product for VAX processors is POLYCENTER Striping for OpenVMS VAX
V2.1.

DEC Disk Striping for OpenVMS AXP V1.5 is available now. It is a layered
product that supports the OpenVMS License Management Facility. License units
for this product are not allocated on a CPU-capacity basis. Each node that
requires access to a stripeset requires a license for striping.

