DEC ODBC DRIVER FOR MS-Windows V1.1

Many businesses are using relational database management systems (RDBMSs)
from multiple vendors. All major RDBMSs use the Structured Query Language
(SQL) to build database applications, but proprietary extensions and
variable functionality make these systems largely incompatible with one
another. Each vendor provides a proprietary desktop application programming
interface (API), which is used to construct client database requests. These
API calls must be incorporated into off-the-shelf and in-house developed
software in order for client database requests to be processed by the
vendor's proprietary RDBMS on the server. It is costly to train programmers
in the use of each of these desktop APIs and to develop and maintain
applications written with multiple APIs.

Digital's DEC ODBC Driver for MS-Windows enables Windows based, ODBC enabled
applications and tools to access data stored in DEC Rdb and other data
sources accessible through Digital's database gateway products. The V1.1
release includes support for new transports (Windows SOCKETS compliant
TCP/IPs and NetWare SPX/IPX), transparent multimedia support, and support
for stored procedures, primary and foreign keys, and additional performance
enhancing ODBC Level 2 calls.

This is a standards based API driver, thus helping to reduce costs for
programmer training, application development, and maintenance. Programmers
need learn only one Windows API for client database requests and use it to
develop and maintain applications that work with relational data from
multiple vendors. MS-Windows users can choose from a large number of
powerful, industry leading end user and application development tools to
access the data they need.

The DEC ODBC Driver for MS-Windows is available now to DEC Rdb, DEC DB
Integrator, and DEC DB Integrator Gateways users as added value either at no
additional charge or at the cost of a media and documentation kit. It is
licensed and packaged with Digital's database server products (it does not
have a shrink-wrapped license) and is distributed with the three products
named, with ACCESSWORKS V2.0, and with such third party ODBC enabled
products as the Powersoft Powerbuilder, Cognos impromptu, Gupta SQL Windows
and Quest (release this spring), and Q+E Software ODBC Driver Kit (also due
for release this spring).

Specific availability is as follows:

o  For current versions of server products with any license type (runtime,
   interactive, or development):
   - The server product Software Product Description conveys to ODBC enabled
     application users the right to use the DEC ODBC Driver for MS-Windows
     and install it on all Windows PCs supported by a DEC Rdb, DEC DB
     Integrator, or DEC DB integrator Gateway license.
   - If you need additional copies of the driver on a floppy, you order the
     media and documentation kit, order number QA-26D*A-HB, which includes
     an RX24 high density floppy with an installation/user guide in Windows
     help format, and an electronic copy of the SPD.

o  For older versions of supported server products with any license type
   (runtime, interactive, or development) that do not include the DEC ODBC
   Driver, you order the QA-26D*A-HB H-kit.

Note that the DEC ODBC Driver product is both ODBC driver and client
connectivity software. The distribution kit includes all the database client
software (including the MS ODBC Driver Manager and the ODBC Administrator
utility) required to permit an ODBC enabled application to access Digital's
database products. The kit uses the normal Windows installation procedure.

In addition to an ODBC enabled application and the DEC ODBC Driver, a
Windows PC requires a network transport product. V1.0 of the DEC ODBC Driver
requires the PATHWORKS for DOS DECnet or TCP/IP client. V1.1 of the DEC ODBC
Driver supports NetWare SPX/IPX and Windows SOCKETS compliant TCP/IPs.

The calls supported by ODBC are divided into three groups: Core, Level 1,
and Level 2. Core calls are the calls specified by the SQL Access Group Call
Level Interface (CLI). These calls represent the lowest common denominator
of database functionality supported by all SQL Access Group member RDBMS
vendors. Level 1 and Level 2 calls utilize database functions not supported
by all vendors' RDBMS.

The DEC ODBC Driver supports SQL-92 compliant DEC SQL, Digital's value added
SQL extensions, all ODBC Core and Level 1 calls, and several performance
enhancing Level 2 calls. It is supported with DEC Rdb V4.2 (and subsequent
versions), DEC DB Integrator V1.0 (and subsequent versions), and the DEC DB
Integrator Gateway family of interoperability products. The SQL/Services
server (included with the DEC Rdb, DEC DB Integrator, and DEC DB Integrator
Gateway products) is required on the OpenVMS server. Both Alpha AXP and VAX
systems are supported as OpenVMS servers.

ODBC is based upon the SQL Access Group CLI specification. ODBC calls accept
as parameters both standards based SQL (SQL Access Group API) and database
vendors' value added extensions of SQL. ODBC calls are used by an
application to connect to a database, prepare and execute SQL data
definition and data manipulation commands, and manage data structures and
requested data sets (cursors). These ODBC calls are passed, via the MS ODBC
Driver Manager, from the application to a database product-specific ODBC
driver on the PC.

The ODBC driver acts as an interface between the MS ODBC Driver Manager and
a database vendor's proprietary client connectivity software on the PC. The
client connectivity software interfaces to a network transport product,
manages the connection to the vendor's RDBMS, passes the application's SQL
commands to it, and receives data from the RDBMS. The ODBC specification
does not specify the formats and protocols required to connect to a
database.

Client hardware requirements include a PC that can run Windows and Ethernet.
Client software requirements include MS-Windows 3.x and one of the following
network stacks:

o  PATHWORKS for DOS (DECnet) V4.0 or later.
o  PATHWORKS for DOS (TCP/IP) V2.0 or later.
o  Windows SOCKETS compliant TCP/IP.
o  NetWare SPX/IPX V3.1.1.1.

Server software requirements include:

