 OHIO STATE SUPERCOMPUTER CENTER EXPLORING HIGH-END COMPUTING OPTIONS
 WITH ALPHA AXP..The Ohio State Supercomputer Center, leaders in Quantum
 Chemistry Research, recently selected Alpha AXP to help solve their
 high-end computing needs. The initial purchase of ten DEC 3000/300's
 operating as a parallel processor will be used for computational
 chemistry problems and graphics. The systems will also be used to
 support the center's teaching of Advanced Visualization System soft-
 ware, cluster, parallel, Trollius/LAM, and vector computing. Charlie
 Bender says "The quantum chemistry problems that we are trying to work
 on have traditionally not taken full advantage of vector style archi-
 tectures because of the amount of temporary data created. We were
 looking for a system that provides a good balance between computational
 speed, memory, and I/O. We are very happy with the cluster directions
 and products from Digital." Digital ALPHA was chosen over other work-
 station class systems because of the architecture and price/
 performance.

