     DIGITAL'S OEM CONTRACT MANUFACTURING SERVICES GROUP SELECTED TO
      BUILD SIGMA DESIGNS ReelMagic MULTIMEDIA PLAYBACK CONTROLLER

 ANAHEIM, CA -- MARCH 1, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
 announced that its OEM Contract Manufacturing Services Group has been
 selected to build multimedia playback controllers for Sigma Designs,
 Inc.  This selection brings to more than a dozen the number of
 companies that have chosen Digital's contract manufacturing services
 since the unit began accepting external contracts in 1991.  The
 announcement was made at the NEPCON Show, which opened here today in
 the Anaheim Convention Center.

 Sigma Designs' multimedia controller for personal computers, called
 ReelMagic, is based on the MPEG (Motion Picture Experts' Group)
 standard.  ReelMagic decompresses and plays back full-screen,
 full-motion video and CD-quality audio from a standard CD-ROM drive.

 Sigma Designs and its ReelMagic product join more than a dozen other
 major companies and some 40 products currently being manufactured by
 Digital Equipment Corporation's OEM Contract Manufacturing Services
 group. Other major contract manufacturing agreements are currently
 held with Hughes Aircraft and Apple Computer. Today, industry analysts
 estimate the worldwide market for contract manufacturing services to be
 between $17B and $20B, growing from ten to 15 percent per year.

 Separately, Digital Equipment Corporation announced it will feature
 Sigma Designs, Inc.'s ReelMagic solution in the Company's Desktop
 Direct PC Catalog, which is published quarterly and mailed to a million
 PC users.

 Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
 client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
 information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage,
 networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
 solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
 today's global marketplace.

