                   DIGITAL EQUIPMENT ANNOUNCES A NEW

            COMPREHENSIVE LINE OF REALTIME EMBEDDED PRODUCTS

 New Product Set Comprises High-Performance Alpha AXP 64-Bit RISC
 Hardware, Industry-First PCI-based VMEbus Boards, Two Realtime UNIX
 Operating Systems And a Suite Of Complementary Solutions Backed By
 Worldwide Support, Integration and Contract Manufacturing Services

 MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 1, 1994 -- Advancing the competitiveness of
 product manufacturers worldwide, Digital Equipment Corporation today
 announced the availability of a new, comprehensive product line of
 realtime embedded computing products. The hardware/software product
 suite, developed specifically to meet the needs of users working with
 realtime embedded applications, represents a milestone for the emerging
 embedded systems market as the first complete product set offering the
 highest performance levels and broadest support for industry standards.

 "We are totally committed to the realtime embedded market with a
 complete organization in place to drive our commitment," says Larry
 Cabrinety, Vice President of the Components and Peripherals Business
 Unit within Digital Equipment Corp.

 In all, the product set includes five core components featuring
 world-class technology -- including Alpha AXP 64-bit microprocessors,
 peripheral chips, PCI-based VME single board computers, realtime UNIX
 operating systems, and a growing portfolio of third-party products.
 Digital will enable users to purchase the products as a complete
 solution or as individual offerings, providing both a modular option as
 well as a flexible migration path to next-generation architectures.

 Specifically, Digital's realtime embedded line consists of the
 following products:

 1.  Alpha AXP 64-bit microprocessors and peripheral chips;
 2.  Two Alpha AXP PCI-based VMEbus single board computers;
 3.  DEC OSF/1 UNIX operating system with comprehensive realtime
     functionality;
 4.  VxWorks for Alpha AXP operating system for embedded realtime
     applications, and;
 5.  A full range of complementary, third-party products.

 Digital's new product set was previewed under non-disclosure to leading
 manufacturers in the spring of 1993. Since then, several major
 corporations and government prime contractors have invested in
 Digital's new embedded products. Among the organizations implementing
 Alpha AXP technology for embedded and realtime applications are
 Raytheon, ABB Systems Control, Landis & Gyr, Teledyne Geotech, Texas
 Instruments, GE Medical and Science Applications International.

 "As product design becomes increasingly complex and technology-driven,
 OEMs will require a high-performance hardware architecture as well as
 scalable and distributed realtime software that handles intricate
 design projects and facilitates the development of next-generation
 imaging, signal processing and telecommunications applications,"  says
 William Armitage, director of  Embedded and Realtime products, a
 segment of Digital's Components and Peripherals Business Unit.

 Single Source Capability Positions Digital Ahead Of Other Embedded
 Providers, Including Intel, Hewlett-Packard,  Motorola, and Sun
 Microsystems:

 According to Armitage, design engineers often have difficulty
 integrating embedded and realtime products from vendors, often within
 mixed computing environments. "As one omprehensive technology and
 service source, Digital will enable design engineers to focus their
 energy on product innovation, instead of juggling integration and
 multivendor relationships," says Armitage.

 Armitage states that these users are eager to establish a long-term
 technology framework -- incorporating advanced architectures,
 object-oriented programming, distributed realtime and other advanced
 technologies -- but lack the necessary vendor vision and support.  "We
 have next-generation technologies available now, which will allow these
 users to migrate quickly and easily with minimal interruption to the
 existing application schematic," says Armitage. In comparison, says
 Armitage, other vendors serving the embedded market have failed to
 provide single source product and service capabilities as well as a
 long-term technology direction to support the increasingly complex,
 time-sensitive embedded computing needs of users and original equipment
 manufacturers (OEMs).

 In addition, Digital offers several customer-oriented business
 practices which support key OEM customer requirements, according to
 Armitage. These business practices include custom design and contract
 manufacturing services, leadership price and price/performance
 products, flexibility in product delivery and warranty, access to
 future technology directions and global support, among others.

 "These business practices are designed to fully support our OEMs,
 enabling them to maintain their technology leadership and competitive
 advantage as well as reduce time-to-market and operational costs," says
 Armitage.

 Furthermore, OEMs have the added security of investment protection and
 product growth and longevity via Alpha AXP and DEC OSF/1 unified UNIX
 systems.  "No other vendor offers this breadth of capabilities to the
 OEM customer," adds Armitage.

 Digital's Future Growth Path For Manufacturing Users Focuses On
 Scalable, Distributed Realtime Technologies:

 Today, Digital is announcing two UNIX realtime operating systems: the
 DEC OSF/1 operating system with comprehensive realtime functionality
 and the VxWorks for Alpha AXP operating system for embedded realtime
 applications.

 The DEC OSF/1 operating system is a full-featured, unified UNIX
 environment for self-hosted realtime applications. It provides
 significant realtime functionality, including priority-based scheduling
 and full kernel preemption as well as support for POSIX realtime
 standards. VxWorks for Alpha AXP software, a joint effort from Digital
 and Wind River Systems, is based on VxWorks 5.1 -- the industry's
 leading realtime software for high-end VMEbus platform applications.

 While migrating VxWorks 5.1 to the Alpha AXP platform, Digital added
 key functional enhancements, including increased support for POSIX
 1003.1b realtime standard and an additional runtime kernel debugger
 from the DEC OSF/1 operating system.

 "Together, these operating systems support the full range of realtime
 applications," says Armitage.

 New Alpha AXP-Based VME Single Board Computers Offer Highly Competitive
 Price/Performance:

 The realtime UNIX software solutions are supported by new Alpha AXP
 hardware offerings: three new Alpha AXP-based VME single board
 computers. The AXPvme line represents the industry's first Peripheral
 Component Interface (PCI)-based VME single board computers, and, in
 addition, offers a highly competitive price/performance differential
 over comparable offerings from Force and Motorola.  The AXPvme line
 supports the DEC OSF/1 operating system and VxWorks for Alpha AXP
 software.

 Development environments for Digital's new realtime and embedded
 hardware and software offerings are available immediately.

 Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
 client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
 information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage,
 networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
 solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
 today's global marketplace.

