 an Ethernet link, from local disk or from ROM. VxWorks for Alpha AXP
 provides access to the full range of Digital's CASE tools and
 COHESIONworX on the DEC OSF/1 host environment.

 OEMs who want a full-function UNIX realtime operating system may select
 DEC OSF/1, which supports the complete set of industry-standard UNIX
 interfaces, including BSD, SVID, OSF, AES, and COSE. Existing UNIX
 applications can be easily ported to DEC OSF/1 on the AXPvme 160, 64
 and 64LC, which are fully binary compatible with all other Alpha AXP
 products running the DEC OSF/1 UNIX operating system.

 Digital has added extensive realtime capabilities to the DEC OSF/1
 operating system, including a fully preemptive kernel and priority-
 based schedules for improved realtime performance in a disk-based
 operating system. Applications are developed on a DEC OSF/1 host system
 and are downline loaded onto the Alpha AXP target system.

