                DIGITAL EQUIPMENT ANNOUNCES STORAGEWORKS
            CAPACITY BREAKTHROUGH FOR DSSI SYSTEMS CUSTOMERS

              Introduces support and expanded StorageWorks
                  for Novell and Sun Markets in Europe

 MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 8, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
 announced a new generation of StorageWorks controller that brings a
 four fold capacity increase to the DSSI cluster environment. The HSD05
 Array Controller provides the ability to expand from 3.57GB to 14.7GB
 of disk storage per DSSI node. As the only DSSI to SCSI controller that
 is StorageWorks compatible, the HSD05 also offers the benefits of
 connectivity for a wide variety of low-cost, industry standard, SCSI
 storage devices including disks, DAT and DLT tape devices plus solid
 state disks.

 At the same time, Digital launched full support and expanded
 StorageWorks offerings for Novell and Sun markets throughout Europe.
 StorageWorks expansion storage solutions, from the desktop to deskside
 to RAID subsystems, are now shipping for PC LANS running Novell Netware
 V3.11 and for Sun systems running SUN/OS and Solaris.

 Charles F. Christ, vice president of Digital's Storage Business Unit,
 said, "StorageWorks expands the storage choices available to DSSI
 customers by quadrupling the capacity previously available to them and
 allowing them to connect multiple SCSI devices to their DSSI clusters
 in the most cost-effective way.  StorageWorks in the DSSI environment
 enables our customers to take advantage of modular, scalable SCSI
 storage solutions while protecting their investments in the DSSI
 architecture. Today's announcement reinforces Digital's goal to provide
 storage solutions at the best price-performance levels in the
 marketplace."

 Digital's European Director, Sales and Marketing, Gerhard Preissl,
 said, "With storage requirements on Novell PC LANs growing at more than
 50% a year, LAN managers need storage solutions that can grow and
 change apace. StorageWorks modular, scalable, open solutions meet that
 need at a very affordable cost."  "In the Sun marketplace," Preissl
 added, "Digital provides more storage solutions than any other vendor.
 StorageWorks for Sun supports disk, tape, optical, solid-state disk and
 RAID storage products, on the desktop or deskside, all in compatible
 enclosures, all most cost-effectively."

 Also announced today:

 *  RRD43 and RRD44, the next generation of industry-standard CDROM
    drives,

    - offering the fastest dual performance CDROMs available in the
       industry

 *  EZ58R 800MB SCSI Solid State Disk - offering the highest capacity
    SCSI SSD available in the industry

 *  KZTSA, TURBOchannel to SCSI adapter, maximum I/O and data processing
    performance for DEC 3000 systems

 *  StorageWorks device and system support upgrades, including QIC and
    8mm tape drives for the desktop, 20GB DLT drives for StorageWorks,
    and Infoserver 1000 for StorageWorks

