 been published already earlier on several occasions, and may be
 obtained from the HPCN Secretariat.

 The Conference is organized by the Foundation HPCN Europe and is
 focused on HPCN users in research and industry. More than 220 papers
 have been submitted from all over the world, e.g. United States,
 Australia, Japan, Russia and nearly every European country. They
 discuss engineering applications from automotive and aerospace,
 computational chemistry, biology and physics, seismic applications,
 manufacturing, material sciences, real time simulations, environmental
