 WORKSHOP ON HIGH PERFORMANCE NETWORKING REQUIREMENTS FOR
 HIGH PERFORMANCE COMPUTING CENTRES
 April 21 in Munich

 The Workshop will present and discuss the interim results of the
 TEN-IBC project responsible for specifying the network reqirements of
 High Performance Computing Centres in preparation for the development
 of Integrated Broadband Communications (IBC) in Europe.

 The project has surveyed over 100 such centres to establish their
 present position (size, capacity, types of platform, applications, and
 users), and to elicit their views with regard to future developments
 and networking needs. The purpose of the Workshop is to present the
 results of this survey, and to seek feedback on some of the conclusions
 that may be drawn, particularly, with regard to future scenarios for
 the development of HPC Centres throughout Europe.

 (More information: Mike Jeffries   mjeffries@octacon.demon.co.uk )

