   NT, Macintosh, and OpenVMS)

o  Prices reduced minimum of 30 percent and pricing structure simplified

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECmessageQ V3.0 enables developers to save time and money in building and
integrating modular, distributed applications on heterogeneous and
multivendor platforms, reducing time to market for software efforts. You can
preserve your current investments in computing platforms and software
applications as you implement your future computing strategies.

DECmessageQ software is the industry leader in message queuing technology
and is production proven in mission critical applications in the
manufacturing, process control, telecommunications, financial, and defense
industries.

The V3.0 release adds server support for new platforms (the DEC OSF/1, IBM
AIX, Sun Solaris, HP RISC, and Windows NT platforms), a high performance
TCP/IP client for MS-Windows, and recoverable messaging for all platforms,
including UNIX and PC DECmessageQ server implementations.

DECmessageQ V3.0 has developed implementations on all the significant open
platforms for UNIX, PCs, and OpenVMS software, including all three operating
systems that run on the high performance Alpha AXP platform (the DEC OSF/1,
Windows NT, and OpenVMS operating systems).

A new DECmessageQ for MS-Windows client implementation provides robust
Windows features such as support for DLLs, Visual Basic, and
WinSockets over multiple TCP/IP stacks. It includes recoverable messaging,
which is especially important to portable and mobile PCs that have
intermittent network connections. This product has been validated with the
RoamAbout Transport TCP/IP product set.

Please note that the use of DECmessageQ Message Recovery Services (MRS), a
feature for guaranteed message delivery that is releasing with the
DECmessageQ V3.0 UNIX and PC server implementations, will interoperate with
MRS on the OpenVMS VAX and AXP platforms in May 1994, when the beta field
test kit of DECmessageQ for OpenVMS (VAX and AXP) V3.0 will be available.

License prices for the entire family of DECmessageQ products have been
reduced a minimum of 30 percent across all levels (desktop, departmental,
and datacenter computing). For more details please see your Digital sales
representative or Digital distributor. All pricing has also been simplified
to three price tiers. Discounts are available on DECmessageQ server and
client implementations, yielding further significant savings.

For further product information, please consult the following Software
Product Descriptions:

o  SPD 34.07: OpenVMS VAX
o  SPD 46.25: OpenVMS AXP
o  SPD 39.25: DECmessageQ for UNIX (all platforms)
o  SPD 47.90: DECmessageQ for Windows NT
o  SPD 53.34: DECmessageQ for Macintosh server
o  SPD 53.35: DECmessageQ for MS-Windows client
o  SPD 39.26: DECmessageQ for Macintosh client
o  SPD 34.06: DECmessageQ for MS-DOS client
o  SPD 34.09: DECmessageQ for OS/2 client

BENEFITS

o  Broadest platform support in the industry.

o  Transports support for TCP/IP, DECnet, and LU6.2 based networks.

o  A simple set of calls (API) common to all platforms.

o  High performance: thousands of messages per second.

o  Interoperability with IBM MVS/CICS and IBM MVS/IMS using APPC LU6.2
   message conversations.

o  Nonblocking, asynchronous communication for time independent processing.

o  Robust development and management tools.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECmessageQ standard software products are orderable now for delivery in
30 days (LU6.2 Services for OpenVMS AXP systems will be available this
summer). DECmessageQ loaner products are available at no charge for 30, 60,
90, and 180 days (QL-<UPI>*9-LB/LC/LD/LE).

