covered by Layered Product Support.

POLYCENTER FILE OPTIMIZER FOR OpenVMS V2.0

System performance can be negatively impacted by fragmented files, so users
want a tool that will ensure data integrity, reduce file fragmentation, and
thus result in reasonable disk performance. Digital's solution for file
fragmentation is the POLYCENTER File Optimizer for OpenVMS V2.0, formerly
called DEC File Optimizer (DFO).

POLYCENTER File Optimizer for OpenVMS V2.0 is a layered software product
that reduces file fragmentation through scheduled defragmentation jobs and
offers the highest possible data integrity. It makes it easier to establish
and manage your defragmentation processes through the addition of a
graphical user interface. In addition to DCL and Motif interfaces, it offers
a choice of platforms: the Alpha AXP and VAX platforms. The POLYCENTER File
Optimizer provides the safety, ease of use, and performance necessary for
your mission critical data.

Enhancements in the V2.0 release include:

o  Enhanced ease of use with the addition of a graphical user interface.
o  Ability to run on OpenVMS AXP systems.
o  Support for mixed OpenVMS cluster environments.
o  Additional flexibility of the SHOW command.

The POLYCENTER File Optimizer provides the following key benefits:

o  Data integrity -- It ensures absolute data integrity through the use of
   the OpenVMS MOVEFILE primitive, which allows the safe movement of files
   on a disk.

o  Enhanced system management productivity -- It provides a "set and forget"
   policy and automated, event based scheduling, thus reducing the amount of
   time spent on these activities.

o  Reduced backup and operator time -- Defragmentation of files improves the
   performance of backup operations. Less operator time and system resource
   usage are required with the use of this product.

o  Better performing disks --  Defragmentation of files improves application
   response time and allows higher disk utilization.

Both the VAX and Alpha AXP versions of POLYCENTER File Optimizer for OpenVMS
V2.0 will be available in May 1994. The POLYCENTER File Optimizer offers
flat priced, unlimited use licensing regardless of processor size. The same
media and documentation kit applies to the VAX and AXP versions; it is also
available on CDROM. POLYCENTER File Optimizer for OpenVMS AXP V2.0 requires
OpenVMS AXP V6.1.

