POLYCENTER DECnet MANAGER ON NetView V1.0 FOR DEC OSF/1 AXP

The POLYCENTER network management portfolio has been expanded to include
POLYCENTER DECnet Manager (SPD 62.53), a DECnet management application
layered on POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for DEC OSF/1 AXP (SPD 53.57), also
known as POLYCENTER NetView. NetView is the industry leading network
management platform.

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager has been developed for users who want to manage
multivendor/multiprotocol networks (DECnet Phase IV, DECnet/OSI, IP, LAT,
ELMS), Digital LAN bridges, terminal servers, and network devices from the
same console. The superior POLYCENTER NetView API (general topology manager)
allows for this integration. (TCP/IP devices are also manageable with
POLYCENTER NetView today.)

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager thus consists of network management applications
to manage Digital's older terminal servers with RC/MOP, DECnet Phase IV with
NICE/NCP, and DECnet/OSI with DNA CHIP using NCC. Additional functionality
that is not specific to network management, such as data collection and
reference data applications, is also included in this product. POLYCENTER
DECnet Manager uses the POLYCENTER NetView leadership user interface and
architecture to enhance user productivity and ease of use.

The 130 members of the NetView Association are developing applications to
expand the choices available to users. These applications can be integrated
with POLYCENTER NetView.

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager provides DECnet management capabilities on a DEC
OSF/1 AXP platform. Users of the DECmcc (POLYCENTER Network Manager 200/400)
and MSU (POLYCENTER SNMP Manager 300) products will be interested in testing
POLYCENTER DECnet Manager, which is the recommended alternative for DECmcc
and MSU users migrating to the DEC OSF/1 AXP platform.

Together with POLYCENTER NetView, POLYCENTER DECnet Manager can fully
DECmcc users. By migrating
to this advanced network management environment, MSU and DECmcc users can
increase their productivity and gain additional capabilities not present in
the DECmcc and MSU products.

To assist in this migration, Digital's product release plans are summarized
below. (The following section provides more detailed information and the
migration options available.) POLYCENTER NetView and POLYCENTER DECnet
Manager will ship with the quarterly DEC OSF/1 layered product Consolidated
Distribution CDROM and on the individual product CDROMs. Schedules and
capabilities are as follows:

o  POLYCENTER NetView V2.1 -- Shipping now on DEC OSF/1 systems. Manages any
   SNMP manageable devices (and includes some DECnet Phase IV management
   capabilities as optional unsupported software).

o  POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V1.0 -- Shipping June 1994 on DEC OSF/1
   systems. Provides autotopology, mapping, and autodiscovery of DECnet
   Phase IV and DECnet/OSI devices that are manageable through NCP; manages
   terminal servers and bridges provides full DECnet Phase IV management
   capabilities.

o  POLYCENTER NetView V3.1 -- Shipping August 1994 on DEC OSF/1 systems,
   March 1995 on Windows NT systems, September 1995 on OpenVMS AXP systems.
   Planned enhancements are hot standby failover, ORACLE, INFORMIX, SYBASE,
   and Rdb OSF/1, in addition to INGRES support. (These databases are
   optional and are not required to run POLYCENTER NetView.)

o  POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.0 -- Shipping December 1994 on DEC OSF/1
   systems, June 1995 on Windows NT systems, September 1995 on OpenVMS AXP
   systems. Enhanced DECnet Phase IV data reporting; management of bridges
   and events; other management capabilities, including DECnet/OSI; object
   status of DECnet environment, autotopology, and data collection.

o  POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V3.0 -- Shipping June 1995 on DEC OSF/1
   systems. Enhanced DECnet Phase IV management capabilities and fuller
   DECnet/OSI support.

