Electronic Data Interchange Update

IN THIS SECTION:

o  DEC/EDI V2.0

o  DEC/EDI FileBridge V1.1

DEC/EDI V2.0

DEC/EDI (Electronic Data Interchange) enables users to electronically
exchange structured business documents with their trading partners, using
ANSI X.12, EDIFACT, TRADACOMS, and other EDI industry standards. The client/
server architecture of DEC/EDI V2.0 enables flexible deployment across an
enterprise to provide an EDI capability to applications hosted on multiple
platforms.

The new features of the V2.0 release are:

o  First availability on the Alpha AXP platform.

o  A significant performance improvement to support enterprise-wide
   deployment.

o  Application clients for DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS systems, using ObjectBroker
   software for connectivity.

o  An MS-Windows based graphical user interface for business manager access
   to enterprise-wide information about trading partner transactions.

o  An integrated FileBridge mapper.

o  Support for the CLEO bisynchronous product for 2780/2780 communications.

o  A HostBridge server for the OpenVMS VAX platform.

DEC/EDI V2.0 uses a client/server architecture to provide EDI services to
local and remote applications. ObjectBroker software is used to link local
and remote DEC/EDI application clients to the DEC/EDI server. Applications
clients are available today for OpenVMS VAX, and OpenVMS AXP, and DEC OSF/1
AXP systems. Application clients for IBM MVS (batch and CICS) and VSE-CICS
platforms, based on DECmessageQ software, are also available.

The DEC/EDI server consists of the following components, which reside on a
single node:

o  DEC/EDI HostBridge software
o  DEC/EDI FileBridge software
o  DEC/EDI translation component
o  DEC/EDI communications components
   - DEC/EDI bisynchronous communications component
   - DEC/EDI OFTP communications component
   - DEC/EDI X.400 and X.435 communications component

The features/benefits of the new release can be summarized as follows:

o  Support for international, national, and industry standards -- Ensures
   consistent, worldwide implementation across all departments and
   divisions.

o  Information transmitted directly or through a number of VANs -- Freedom
   to choose the most appropriate connection based on business rather than
   technology restraints.

o  Management, tracking, and routing features -- Provide data and
   interchange integrity from beginning to end of the EDI process.

o  MS-Windows based graphical user interface -- Provides enterprise-wide
   access to EDI transaction status information from the most popular
   desktop environments.

o  Significant improvement in performance and new application clients -- Key
   support for enterprise-wide deployment.

DEC/EDI V2.0 is available now (the HostBridge server will be available in
June 1994). The options listed below are also available, each including the
communications component, the application client, the FileBridge runtime
software, and the translation component required for deployment on a single
