DEC/EDI FileBridge V1.1

The DEC/EDI FileBridge product is a table driven "mapper" that provides a
file based interface for integrating your business applications into a
DEC/EDI solution.

You define the application file and the parameters for mapping from the
application file to the EDI standard through a forms based user interface.
>From this information, FileBridge software generates a conversion table that
is used to map data automatically from/to the application file formats.

FileBridge mapping allows fields to simply be moved or to have predefined
mathematical or logical operations to be performed upon them. Further
flexibility is available: you can define and add code through "hooks" for
more complex processing.

The new features of the V1.1 release:

o  Improved memory management, supporting the processing of documents up to
   20 Mbytes in size.

o  Enhanced support for floating notes.

o  Enhanced support for the callable interface.

o  Support for the License Management Facility (LMF).

o  Worldwide support and software product services.

With these features, DEC/EDI FileBridge V1.1 provides the following
benefits:

o  Reduces or eliminates the programming effort required to integrate
   applications into a DEC/EDI solution, by providing 4GL data mapping
   techniques and processing a wide breadth of file structures and data
   types.

o  Reduces maintenance costs and enables a quicker response to trading
   partner and standards evolution, by isolating trading partner and
   standards specific functionality from the business application.

o  Caters to user specific processing needs via built-in mathematical and
   logical operations.

o  Includes "hook routines" to facilitate the linking of user provided code.

DEC/EDI FileBridge V1.1 is available now.

