DECmigrate V1.2 FOR DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.0 SYSTEMS

DECmigrate V1.2 for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems (SPD 39.45.02) provides a fast and
relatively inexpensive path for migrating from RISC ULTRIX to DEC OSF/1 AXP
systems. It is unique in the industry in translating compiled, user mode
(nonprivileged) RISC ULTRIX applications directly into their DEC OSF/1 AXP
equivalents.

Runtime support for translated images is included with the DEC OSF/1
operating system. This means that the DECmigrate and Alpha AXP combination
can supply RISC ULTRIX behavior when required, without slowing down the
whole application with emulation.

How robust is the translated application? If the input application meets
translation criteria, the translated version is its duplicate; translation
does not introduce software errors.

Note that translation is better than emulation, because translating an
application allows it to take advantage of all the possible performance
gains that the Alpha AXP platform provides. Note also that DECmigrate
software can generate a working translation for most user mode RISC ULTRIX
applications that were compiled on a DECsystem or DECstation RISC system
running ULTRIX V4.0 or later. For a list of specific restrictions, see the
Software Product Description.

Many translated applications run faster on Alpha AXP systems than they ran
native. The only way to make them even faster is to port. With DECmigrate
V1.2, you can stage your transition to the Alpha AXP environment by
translating your user mode applications now and porting from source later.

DECmigrate V1.2 is the preferred migration solution when time is short or
resources are lacking for source code migration. DECmigrate translation is
the only migration solution when:

o  Source code is not available for all components.

o  Language support for some components is not yet available on the DEC
   OSF/1 AXP system.

o  Source code assumes that pointers and long integers are 32 bits wide, and
   these assumptions cannot be readily corrected.

DECmigrate V1.2 will be available with a full, unlimited user license,
concurrently with the release of DEC OSF/1 V2.0. The DECmigrate binaries and
documentation will be available on the DEC OSF/1 V2.0 Layered Products CDROM
and also as an H-kit.

