Calendar Manager for Macintosh, Windows, and ALL-IN-1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Calendar Manager V4.0 for Macintosh users, providing group scheduling for
   TeamLinks for Macintosh users

o  Calendar Manager V5.0 for Windows and ALL-IN-1 VT users

o  Introductory pricing extended to June 30, 1994

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Calendar Manager, from Russell Information Sciences, is a client/server
software package (SPD 53.29) that supports both individual time management
requirements and group scheduling requirements. The time management
capability includes daily, weekly, and monthly calendar planning. It also
supports "to-do lists" and "tickler" notices of scheduled events/items. The
scheduling capabilities enable workgroups to schedule meetings, events, and
facilities across the local workgroup, with another networked workgroup, or
across the enterprise.

The Calendar Manager for Macintosh V4.0 client delivers all these
capabilties to Macintosh users, plus full interoperability with TeamLinks
for Windows and ALL-IN-1 VT users. (The Calendar Manager for Macintosh V5.0
client will be available later this year.)

Calendar Manager V5.0 for Windows and ALL-IN-1 VT users offers several new
capabilities. Key enhancements in this release include:

o  A new Executive Diary user interface (available only to Microsoft Windows
   users) is an alternative to the original Month window and provides an
   intuitive, drag-and-drop interface. This format lets you view Calendar
   in a graphical daily planner representation in either a single or dual
   tab mode. The diary has five tabs (Day, Week, View, To-Do, List).

o  A new ability to view the system-wide distribution lists on your system
   (DOS and terminal users only).

o  A new feature that allows you to delegate ownership to a specified user
   who is either a confirmed attendee of the scheduled meeting or has full
   proxy access to your calendar.

o  Additional customization options. You can enter in your own work start
   time, which will affect all displays in Calendar Manager that have fixed
   time-slot formats: Day window, Weekly Summary, Quick View window, and Day
   Tab--Executive Diary (Windows clients only). In addition, you can set the
   time increments to show either 5, 10, 15, 20, 30, or 60 minutes in the
   Day window, Weekly Summary, Quick View window, and Day Tab--Executive
   Diary.

o  You now have the option of attaching a message when responding to a
   meeting request. A meeting can have multiple notes attached.

o  A new option to undo rejected/canceled attendance lets you recover any
   meeting(s) you have rejected in the past.

o  A new subject field default list lets you add subjects to your drop-down
   subject list.

BENEFITS

o  If you are an ALL-IN-1 IOS or TeamLinks user, you can move your terminals
   and PCs to a robust group scheduling application, taking advantage of
   Calendar Manager's full integration with the ALL-IN-1 and TeamLinks
   solutions.

o  A common group scheduling application for PC, Macintosh, and VT users
   ensures the ability of people to work together independently of the
   desktop they are using.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Calendar Manager can be ordered now. Both the V4.0 and V5.0 releases will be
available in late April. All platform licenses processed through June 30,
1994, can take advantage of a special introductory offer (30 percent off).

